    "summary": "Goal: add dev-only quality tooling (ruff lint, mypy type check) and golden CLI output tests as the safety net for the F1.0.3 module split, without changing the shipped skill's behaviour. Scope: tool configuration in a repo-root pyproject.toml (dev only, no packaging), pinned dev requirements file, a CI job running ruff and mypy, golden tests for workflow.py --help and per-command help, status, spec-check, plan-check, outcome and init --discover --json (normalized for temp paths, times and machine-specific tool presence), with an explicit regeneration switch. Exclusions: no runtime dependency, nothing new inside the skill folder, no behaviour change, no refactoring beyond mechanical lint fixes (unused names, import order) proven safe by the full suite and the golden tests. Affected areas: pyproject.toml (new), requirements-dev.txt (new), tests/test_golden.py and tests/golden/ (new), .github/workflows/tests.yml, possibly lint-only edits in workflow.py, install.py, tests and tools. Existing: no linter or type checker configured (TD-17); tests drive workflow.main() in-process with an isolated home (tests/helpers.py)."
  },
